WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.449
The prologue of The Conjuring 2 takes place
a year before the main events of the movie

00:00:03.449 --> 00:00:06.530
and contains the key to understanding the
secret to the film’s ending.

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:09.930
Our first shot introduces us to the Amityville
house, and you’ll notice the wallpaper of

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:14.610
this upstairs room depicts images from the
1967 play Not Now, Darling, a story set in

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:17.860
Great Britain, which would also be where Ed
and Lorraine Warren would finally have their

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:22.140
confrontation with the inhuman spirit, Valak,
who is teased at in secret in the background

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:25.820
of many scenes, so stick around to the end
of this video to hear about all of them.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:29.140
But before our heroes would travel across
the pond, they have to deal with this haunting

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:30.140
on Long Island.

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:33.250
This is the case set up at the end of the
first movie, when Ed and Lorraine get a call

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:37.040
to go investigate the house of the Lutz family,
who were haunted by the ghosts of the DeFeos,

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:41.280
a family who was brutalized by Ronnie DeFeo
Jr. who claimed to be under the influence

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.780
of a demonic presence when he committed his
crimes.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:47.360
Lorraine has an out of body experience where
she travels through the house and sees into

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:48.879
the past to that fatal night.

00:00:48.879 --> 00:00:52.290
She’s seeing these atrocities take place
through the viewpoint of Ronnie DeFeo.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:55.920
We can tell because Lorraine’s reflection
in the mirror is replaced with that of Ronnie.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.719
So Lorraine is using Ronnie’s ghost as a
vessel so she can gain more information about

00:00:59.719 --> 00:01:03.530
the past -- and this same concept is used
against her in England, where the demon Valak

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:07.737
hides behind the lingering spirit of this
old man so that Lorraine is unable to detect

00:01:07.737 --> 00:01:08.237
it.

00:01:08.237 --> 00:01:11.709
At the end of her projection, she follows
one of the DeFeo children into the basement.

00:01:11.709 --> 00:01:15.599
There she discovers a couple of mannequins,
which are a signature of director James Wan,

00:01:15.599 --> 00:01:18.789
as seen in Saw, Dead Silence and Insidious:
Chapter 2.

00:01:18.789 --> 00:01:22.770
But more importantly she encounters Valak,
who attacks her shortly before she has a vision

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:24.189
of a man’s neck cracking.

00:01:24.189 --> 00:01:28.099
However, if we go back to that scene and turn
up the lights, we can actually see that it’s

00:01:28.099 --> 00:01:32.289
her husband, Ed, leading her to fear for his
life just as he feared for hers in the first

00:01:32.289 --> 00:01:35.259
movie, which, by the way, comes back around
here in the sequel.

00:01:35.259 --> 00:01:38.919
In the first one, Ed is wary of getting involved
in anything paranormal because of an intense

00:01:38.919 --> 00:01:42.409
vision that took a huge toll on Lorraine in
1970.

00:01:42.409 --> 00:01:47.709
“A couple months ago we were working on
a case, she saw something.

00:01:47.709 --> 00:01:49.880
It took a real big piece.”

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:52.420
...and this is confirmed to be Valak in The
Conjuring 2.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:54.209
“I had a vision in Amityville.

00:01:54.209 --> 00:01:56.950
It was the same one I had 7 years ago.”

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:01.020
So Valak is the big antagonist that has been
built up from the beginning of the franchise.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:04.698
To learn all of it’s hidden secrets, stick
around to the end of this video.

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:10.920
Welcome to Things You Missed.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:13.959
In today’s episode, it should be obvious
by now what movie I’m covering.

00:02:13.959 --> 00:02:17.910
This is at least one of my top 3 Christmas
movies and probably one of the scariest movies

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:18.410
I’ve seen.

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:21.730
There was a lot of excitement in the horror
community when it was announced that the second

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:25.630
Conjuring would focus on the infamous Enfield
Poltergeist, one of the most highly debated

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:27.910
paranormal investigations of all time.

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:31.690
If you look at the supposed paranormal activity
caught on tape today, it’s pretty obvious

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:35.219
how everything was faked, but the sheer amount
of people involved who claimed to believe

00:02:35.219 --> 00:02:38.470
that something supernatural was happening
is enough to raise an eyebrow.

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:42.310
The movie introduces the idea that the demon
forced the young girl, Janet, to fake an incident

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:45.560
to shatter her credibility with the press,
which was probably inspired by the theory

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:49.220
in real life that the girls started faking
certain things once they saw how much attention

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:53.040
the real paranormal events garnered them;
and the main investigator, Maurice Grosse,

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:54.560
still believed the haunting to be genuine.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:58.475
There’s a lot to unpack here, so let’s
jump back into the Things You Missed.

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:08.329
With the sounds of The Clash, we are transported
into 1977 England, where we’re introduced

00:03:08.329 --> 00:03:09.569
to the Hodgson family.

00:03:09.569 --> 00:03:13.340
The girl who is most associated with the poltergeist
is 11 year old Janet, and she gets caught

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:16.540
smoking a cigarette at school, but she was
actually just holding it for her friend.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.290
However, none of the adults believe her.

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:21.590
They are shown to be hypocrites, scolding
her for her behaviour while engaging in the

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:22.959
same behaviour themselves.

00:03:22.959 --> 00:03:26.020
This is the perfect character introduction
for Janet, because nobody believes she’s

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:29.239
telling the truth due to her age, which is
exactly what happens when she becomes involved

00:03:29.239 --> 00:03:32.620
in the hauntings, making the situation seem
that much more hopeless for her.

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:36.319
There’s actually a deleted scene, where
Ed, Lorraine and Maurice discuss the possibility

00:03:36.319 --> 00:03:40.299
of Janet being possessed with Mrs. Hodgson,
and Ed brings up an interesting point about

00:03:40.299 --> 00:03:41.299
Janet’s age.

00:03:42.679 --> 00:03:44.500
PEGGY: “What about Janet?

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:45.352
I want to know.

00:03:45.352 --> 00:03:46.346
Is she possessed?

00:03:46.346 --> 00:03:48.099
ED: “It’s too soon to say.

00:03:48.099 --> 00:03:50.359
The onset of puberty, the fracturing of the
family.

00:03:50.359 --> 00:03:53.090
These are things that can definitely attract
a negative energy.”

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:56.840
This is actually a real phenomenon -- the
majority of poltergeist claims do involve

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:58.029
pubescent aged kids.

00:03:58.029 --> 00:04:01.630
Ed’s explanation is that the spirits are
drawn to the negative emotions associated

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:05.049
with hitting puberty, which in Janet’s case
are heightened by the fact that her parents

00:04:05.049 --> 00:04:06.190
recently went through a divorce.

00:04:06.190 --> 00:04:11.120
But the opposite argument can be made, rationalists
will say that because of their puberty experience,

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:14.690
these kids are lashing out and creating these
so called “paranormal” spectacles as an

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:16.060
attention seeking method.

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:19.060
So this dichotomy is part of the central conflict
in the movie.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:22.490
After returning home from school, Janet and
her older sister, Margaret, test out the spirit

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:25.810
board that Janet and her friend made, which
is perhaps what opened their family up to

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:26.504
the haunting.

00:04:26.504 --> 00:04:29.060
But I’m sure if you order this tee 
using the link in the description, you’ll

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:30.250
probably be fine.

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:33.930
Specifically, they ask if their father is
ever coming back, and this might have attracted

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:37.610
the inhuman spirit because it sensed it could
feed off of this negative energy.

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:39.930
Sure enough, that night, scary stuff starts
to happen.

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:43.330
Janet wakes up on the floor in front of the
supposedly haunted chair in the living room

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:46.456
and Margaret is woken up by three loud knocks
on their bedroom door.

00:04:46.456 --> 00:04:47.670
*KNOCK KNOCK KNOCK*

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:51.320
There are a few instances in the movie where
the poltergeist tries to scare them by knocking

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:54.550
in threes, like a couple nights later later,
when Janet is pulled out of bed...

00:04:54.550 --> 00:04:55.769
*KNOCK KNOCK KNOCK*

00:04:55.769 --> 00:04:59.970
...and when the police come to investigate, and experience
the paranormal activity for themselves.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:00.970
*KNOCK KNOCK KNOCK*

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:04.371
The reason that the knocks always come in
threes goes back to a minor detail from the

00:05:04.371 --> 00:05:05.371
first Conjuring.

00:05:06.596 --> 00:05:09.310
ROGER: “Oh, that’s to keep those doors
from banging at night.

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:13.967
Otherwise it’s like… all night long, just
like that.”

00:05:13.967 --> 00:05:15.319
ED: “Does it come in threes?”

00:05:15.319 --> 00:05:16.319
“Yeah.”

00:05:16.319 --> 00:05:20.355
“Sometimes it’s meant as an insult to
the trinity, the father, the son and holy

00:05:20.355 --> 00:05:21.110
spirit.”

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:25.139
The night after Janet wakes up downstairs,
even more weird stuff starts to occur, like

00:05:25.139 --> 00:05:28.780
a swing in the backyard moving on it’s own
and Janet talking in her sleep.

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:33.020
Margaret notices this and witnesses her sister
turn towards the dark corner of the room,

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:36.190
apparently possessed by the spirit of the
home’s previous owner, Bill Wilkins.

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:39.720
It’s almost like she’s having a conversation
with someone in this corner, but when Margaret

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:43.210
goes to investigate, there’s no one there,
despite the fact that all the posters on the

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:46.099
walls make it feel like many pairs of eyes
are watching them.

00:05:46.099 --> 00:05:50.330
But this is the exact spot where Valak would
spawn at the end of the movie and during that

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:54.120
final scene, we get our only short glimpse
at the demon’s true form, whose origins

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.467
will be explored later in this video.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:09.240
The Hodgson family’s initial diagnosis of
their situation is that they’re being haunted

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:13.020
by the ghost of Bill Wilkins, the old man
who allegedly died in this chair before the

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:14.069
Hodgsons moved in.

00:06:14.069 --> 00:06:17.389
When Billy Hodgson wanders downstairs for
a glass of water during the night, you can

00:06:17.389 --> 00:06:21.270
spot the ghost of Bill Wilkins, sitting in
the chair as he passes by the living room.

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:23.889
Back in Connecticut, The Warrens start having
visions about Valak.

00:06:23.889 --> 00:06:27.000
In my episode on the first Conjuring movie,
I mentioned that the paintings seen around

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:30.830
the house are a nod to the real life Ed Warren,
who created sketches of people’s homes as

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:34.823
a gift in order to start a conversation about
any supernatural happenings the owners might

00:06:34.823 --> 00:06:35.455
have experienced.

00:06:35.455 --> 00:06:39.110
It seems that he also just enjoys painting
as a hobby, because in his office later in

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:42.039
the movie, there’s a picture of the Perron
family home from the Conjuring.

00:06:42.039 --> 00:06:46.160
But this time Ed paints a creepy nun from
his dream, perhaps a sign that he too has

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:50.139
a little bit of clairvoyant ability, maybe
just nowhere as strong as Lorraine.

00:06:50.139 --> 00:06:53.919
Lorraine recognizes The Nun from her previous
visions but does not know it’s name.

00:06:53.919 --> 00:06:57.979
In The Conjurverse, knowing a demon’s name
gives an exorcist dominion over it.

00:06:57.979 --> 00:07:01.009
However, if you’re paying attention to the
background details of many scenes, you’ll

00:07:01.009 --> 00:07:05.229
see creepy signs of the demons name, Valak,
hidden around the house in secret.

00:07:05.229 --> 00:07:10.430
In the kitchen, this loVe ornament has a capital
V, and the letters A-L-A-K are hidden on this

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:11.430
panel.

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:15.169
By the window, there’s some artwork by their
daughter, Judy, which also spell out the name:

00:07:15.169 --> 00:07:16.169
Valak.

00:07:16.169 --> 00:07:18.810
Then in the Warren’s study, there are a
series of letters arranged on the bookshelf.

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:21.750
If you read them from left to right, you’ll
see V-A-L-A-K.

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:24.810
There’s also a small nun ornament on that
shelf.

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:28.629
During this scene, Judy is making bracelets,
and if you zoom in, one of them says Valak

00:07:28.629 --> 00:07:29.629
on it.

00:07:29.629 --> 00:07:32.409
This is a couple times where the name has
appeared in Judy’s art, and I think it’s

00:07:32.409 --> 00:07:36.199
a subtle sign that she too has the abilities
of a medium like Lorraine, which is backed

00:07:36.199 --> 00:07:39.850
up in the next scene where she is able to
see Valak in the hallway, though, I guess

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:43.229
it’s debatable if this is just part of Lorraine’s
dream, but it does seem like they’ve been

00:07:43.229 --> 00:07:46.939
setting up the idea of Judy possibly being
a medium and getting her own movie in the

00:07:46.939 --> 00:07:47.439
future.

00:07:47.439 --> 00:07:49.189
A couple notes on this scene by the way.

00:07:49.189 --> 00:07:52.620
This has got to be an homage to the twins
scene in the Shining, which also has a kid

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:56.620
having a vision of a scary entity at the end
of a long hallway with flower wallpaper.

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:59.909
I just love how the Warrens have this wallpaper
going all the way down, but they also felt

00:07:59.909 --> 00:08:02.740
the need to put up these framed photos of…
the same flowers.

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:06.490
But while Lorraine is in the study, she’s
studying her bible, and she has it open to

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:08.710
a page with the headline: The Song of Solomon.

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:12.349
This is an interesting detail, because there
are two demons we’ve met up to this point

00:08:12.349 --> 00:08:16.170
in The Conjuring franchise, Malthus, the main
antagonist of the Annabelle spin-offs and

00:08:16.170 --> 00:08:17.650
Valak from this movie.

00:08:17.650 --> 00:08:21.780
Both of these demons come from this 17th Century
spellbook said to contain rituals for summoning

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:23.669
demons called The Lesser Key of Solomon.

00:08:23.669 --> 00:08:28.090
They’re based off of Halphas and Valac respectively,
who are both supposedly Presidents of Hell.

00:08:28.090 --> 00:08:32.140
The mythological version of Valac is never
associated with a Nun form, that was an invention

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:34.030
of the film’s director, James Wan.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:37.120
The initial vision for Valak was actually
more in line with the traditional appearance

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:40.890
of a demon, but this look was mostly scrapped
in favor of having Valak appear as a creepy

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:44.470
nun, which fits nicely with the idea that
the evil entity is attacking Lorraine’s

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:47.400
faith, the same reason for the three knocks
that I mentioned earlier.

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:51.231
However, we do still see a remnant of the
initial design for Valak at the end, after

00:08:51.231 --> 00:08:55.140
Lorraine has condemned the creature back to
hell, it convulses and briefly reverts back

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:58.070
to it’s true form before being sucked back
into the underworld.

00:08:58.070 --> 00:09:01.310
I’ll turn up the lights again so you can
get a better look at the villain's actual

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:02.310
appearance.

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:06.260
I also want to note that in the real life
Enfield poltergeist case, the family did allegedly

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:09.870
suspect the old man Bill Wilkins being the
spirit that was haunting them, but there was

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:13.620
never anything about him being controlled
by Valak, that’s strictly in the movie.

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:17.260
When Lorraine has the vision about Valak in
the study, she envisions Valak attacking her

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:21.156
in Ed’s office, and she’s startled by
the stereo suddenly turning on...

00:09:21.156 --> 00:09:25.000
🎵 Hark the Herald Angels Sing 🎵

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:29.310
...and playing the Christmas song “Hark the Herald
Angels Sing”, which is a British song, perhaps

00:09:29.310 --> 00:09:32.940
a clue that her encounter with Valak would
be in England around Christmastime.

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:36.410
We do hear that song during the finale when
Ed tries to save Janet.

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:40.801
🎵 Hark the Herald Angels Sing 🎵

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:44.880
The vision continues with Valak manifesting
behind Ed’s painting and attacking her,

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:48.510
during which she falls and knocks over this
holy statue thing, another symbol of the demon

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:50.220
trying to attack her faith.

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:53.220
When she gets up she finds herself back in
the basement in Amityville…

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:55.000
“WHO ARE YOU?”

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:56.756
“I’m spiderman.”

00:09:56.756 --> 00:10:00.690
And when she awakes from the vision, she subconsciously
scribbles somethings onto the pages of her

00:10:00.690 --> 00:10:05.970
bible, if you're paying close attention you see her write the letters V-A-L
before it cuts away, but because she’s still

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:09.210
in her vision, she doesn’t realize that
she’s discovered the demon’s name.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:12.820
There’s also a crossword puzzle next to
her when she comes to, a possible sign that

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:17.310
she needs this missing word, Valak, in order to have
dominion over the evil spirit.

00:10:17.310 --> 00:10:20.960
Finally, when Ed and Lorraine do finally get
to England, they meet with Maurice and a couple

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:24.590
others who are involved in the investigation
at The Warrington Pub, and the drink coasters

00:10:24.590 --> 00:10:26.790
have text reading: Valak Bitter.

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:29.380
There are signs other than just those about
Valak.

00:10:29.380 --> 00:10:33.290
For example, the toy train in Billy’s room
could foreshadow the train ride where Ed finally

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:37.670
realizes that Bill Wilkins’s spirit is being
controlled and the Humpty Dumpty toy on Janet

00:10:37.670 --> 00:10:40.910
and Margaret’s dresser is one of the few
toys to remain in the room after everything

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:43.700
is cleared out in an attempt to sanitize the
evil presence.

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:47.470
As you may know, Humpty Dumpty had a great
fall, and Ed Warren nearly shares the same

00:10:47.470 --> 00:10:48.780
fate at the end of the movie.

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:52.190
Whoa, Janet, wait till you get older before
you get into that stuff!

00:10:52.190 --> 00:10:55.850
Before long, a news program gave a report
on the Green Street house, and the story started

00:10:55.850 --> 00:10:57.120
to blow up in the media.

00:10:57.120 --> 00:10:59.730
One of the interviewees on this news program
is named Hazel Short.

00:10:59.730 --> 00:11:01.500
She’s based off of a real life person.

00:11:01.500 --> 00:11:05.430
Hazel Short was a lollipop lady, which is
apparently British for crossing guard.

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:10.161
“I saw Janet laying flat.

00:11:10.161 --> 00:11:12.170
And she was floating.

00:11:12.170 --> 00:11:17.150
She was going up and down in front of the
bedroom window.”

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:20.140
Graham Morris was also a real photographer
from The Daily Mirror,

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:25.080
“I used to work for the daily mirror as
a general news photographer.

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:31.120
I think the crunch came when the person on
the phone yelled out and said, ‘Oh, well

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:34.020
we’ve all seen this, including the police.’”

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:35.490
We’re related.

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:36.490
Not really.

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:38.760
I mean I don’t actually know… but I know
deep down that we are…

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:41.970
The Constables who took down the report really
did give a documentary interview.

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:48.400
“It came off the floor maybe a half inch,
I’d say, and I saw it slide off to the right

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:50.580
about three and a half to four feet.”

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:54.690
And the interview scene, of course, was based
on actual interviews given by the girls in

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:55.860
1977.

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:59.580
One detail I found interesting was how in
the movie, Margaret essentially says the opposite

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:01.270
of what she said in real life.

00:12:02.526 --> 00:12:05.110
REPORTER: “How does it feel living in a
haunted house?”

00:12:05.110 --> 00:12:06.540
MARGARET: “I don’t know.

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:08.678
You don’t get used to it.

00:12:08.678 --> 00:12:11.880
We was just a normal family before this.”

00:12:12.615 --> 00:12:15.436
REPORTER: “How does it feel to be haunted
by a poltergeist?”

00:12:15.436 --> 00:12:16.660
JANET: “It’s not haunted.”

00:12:16.660 --> 00:12:17.751
MARGARET: “Shut up….”

00:12:17.751 --> 00:12:20.312
REPORTER: “Does it frighten you, the things
that happen here?”

00:12:20.312 --> 00:12:25.080
MARGARET: “Well it did at first, but now
I’ve gotten more used to it, and learned

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:26.820
to accept the things that happen.”

00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:30.620
I find it ironic how the movie will take such
great lengths to get the little details right

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:34.370
when recreating these videos, but then completely
exaggerate how much the Warrens were actually

00:12:34.370 --> 00:12:35.790
involved in the story.

00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:39.490
Apparently they were only actually there for
a day or two off the 2 year investigation.

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:42.610
There would be more well documented reports
in the media that we can compare to their

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:46.067
real life counterparts and discover even more
Things You Missed.

00:12:54.802 --> 00:12:58.380
Ed and Lorraine first learn of the Enfield
poltergeist when their priest plays them the

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:02.560
audio recording of Bill Wilkins supposedly
taking over Janet Hodgson’s voice.

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:03.730
BILL: “Knock, knock.”

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:07.180
MAURICE: “Very vell, who’s there?”

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:11.439
BILL: “Bill. Bill. Bill. Bill!"

00:13:11.439 --> 00:13:15.118
🎵 "Bill! Bill! Bill! Bill! Bill Nye the science guy!” 🎵

00:13:15.118 --> 00:13:18.480
Word was getting around quickly about the
terror on Green Street, and the Daily Mirror

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:22.660
headline seen in the movie is a recreation
of an actual newspaper front page from September

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:27.140
10th, 1977, but it seems James Wan wanted
the bit about Shore’s son taken out.

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:28.430
Not sure what that’s about.

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:32.470
When the Warrens arrive in the UK, the conduct
a test to see if Janet is really the one making

00:13:32.470 --> 00:13:35.340
the demonic voices, or if she’s actually
being possessed.

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:38.840
In the true story, this is one of the most
debated aspects of the conversation.

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:42.360
There was some disagreement about whether
it would be possible to Janet’s larynx to

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:45.784
produce that noise, and whether she would
be able to keep it up for long periods of

00:13:45.784 --> 00:13:46.386
time.

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:50.572
REPORTER: “Do you think there’s anyone
there just now?”

00:13:50.572 --> 00:13:52.191
JANET: “Yeah.

00:13:52.191 --> 00:13:54.178
I do.”

00:13:56.030 --> 00:13:58.160
REPORTER: “Who’s there?”

00:13:59.446 --> 00:14:00.866
JANET: “What?”

00:14:00.866 --> 00:14:04.450
ED: “Am I talking to the spirit that’s
oppressing this family?”

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:06.526
BILL: “Is that what I am?”

00:14:06.526 --> 00:14:10.470
That night, there’s another clue that Bill
Wilkins in merely a pawn being controlled

00:14:10.470 --> 00:14:11.302
by Valak.

00:14:11.302 --> 00:14:15.230
Janet is transported from downstairs into
her locked room in the middle of night, and

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:18.690
she sees all the crosses on the walls invert
in a circle around her.

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:22.580
This follows the same motion that we saw earlier
when the Nun’s shadow circled around Lorraine

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:23.810
during her vision.

00:14:23.810 --> 00:14:29.267
Unfortunately, this technique gets kinda overused
in the later spin-offs The Nun and Annabelle Comes Home.

00:14:29.267 --> 00:14:33.470
The one monster I haven’t mentioned yet
is The Crooked Man, who is a physical manifestation

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:36.120
of the character from Billy’s nursery rhyme
zoetrope toy.

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:40.040
It isn’t exactly spelled out if this is
Valak, or another character entirely.

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:43.820
I’m guessing it’s a separate entity that’s
being manipulated by Valak in a similar way

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:48.070
to how Bill was manipulated, because you can
actually see The Crooked Man lurking in the

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:51.200
background here as Ed goes to try to save
Janet from Valak’s clutches.

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:54.570
There’s been some talk about a possible
Crooked Man spin-off movie, but it’s hard

00:14:54.570 --> 00:14:57.460
to say if that’s still coming in the wake
of a global pandemic.

00:14:57.460 --> 00:15:00.930
At the beginning of this video I talked about
how alleged poltergeists are often heavily

00:15:00.930 --> 00:15:04.940
associated with the negative energy of kids
hitting their pubescent years and oftentimes

00:15:04.940 --> 00:15:08.890
are the result of a troubled home life, and
it seems that The Conjuring 2 acknowledges

00:15:08.890 --> 00:15:12.810
that tendency, because The Warrens are only
able confront Valak and finally send it away

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:16.317
after helping The Hodgson's return to a sense
of normalcy in their family.

00:15:16.317 --> 00:15:19.190
"In the meantime, Ed and I can be spending
time with Peggy and the kids.

00:15:19.190 --> 00:15:21.260
Cause they need to be a family again."

00:15:21.260 --> 00:15:24.790
One of the reasons they are struggling is
the divorce, which was potentially what caused

00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:27.390
the dark spirit to come into their lives in
the first place.

00:15:27.390 --> 00:15:30.310
"Is Dad ever coming home?"

00:15:30.310 --> 00:15:34.500
So it's probably no coincidence that Ed and
Lorraine are what drive their demon away,

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:36.320
it’s both literal and figurative.

00:15:36.320 --> 00:15:39.370
Peggy tells Ed that when her husband left
he took the music with him.

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:41.020
“No literally, he took all the records.

00:15:41.020 --> 00:15:43.640
My kids used to love listening to his Elvis
collection.”

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:47.420
So by Ed buying them new Elvis albums and
performing his music for the kids, he’s

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:50.930
kind of filling the fatherly role -- he’s
helping this family patch up the void left

00:15:50.930 --> 00:15:54.910
by the missing father and presumably weakening
the hold that Valak has on the family.

00:15:54.910 --> 00:15:56.040
“Thank you.”

00:15:56.040 --> 00:15:57.040
*laugher*

00:15:57.040 --> 00:16:00.511
He also helps soften the damage of the lack
of father figure by helping Peggy out when

00:16:00.511 --> 00:16:03.020
the laundry room in their building is flooded.

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:04.020
“Alright.

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:04.905
There we go.”

00:16:04.905 --> 00:16:05.718
Ah, yes.

00:16:05.718 --> 00:16:06.459
Ed Warren.

00:16:06.459 --> 00:16:07.214
Plumber.

00:16:07.214 --> 00:16:07.834
Mechanic.

00:16:07.834 --> 00:16:08.755
Musician.

00:16:08.755 --> 00:16:09.387
Painter.

00:16:09.387 --> 00:16:10.000
Husband.

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:10.622
Father.

00:16:10.622 --> 00:16:11.122
Priest.

00:16:11.122 --> 00:16:12.000
And oh, yeah…

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:13.361
Paranormal Investigator.

00:16:13.361 --> 00:16:17.730
But this time it would be Lorraine that saved
Ed by sending Valak back to the depths of

00:16:17.730 --> 00:16:20.690
hell and pulling him to safety, just before
he fell to his death.

00:16:20.690 --> 00:16:24.180
The Warrens place the Crooked Man zoetrope
in their room of cursed objects right next

00:16:24.180 --> 00:16:27.720
to the music box from the first movie and
the Warrens celebrate Christmas with a little

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:28.720
bit of the King.

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:29.720
Happy ending.

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:33.510
Roll the credits, because there are a few
more subliminal Things You Missed hidden inside

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:34.010
them.

00:16:34.010 --> 00:16:38.930
The first is this image, which only flashes
on screen for one frame, or 1/24th of a second,

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:42.600
where we see Valak in it’s Nun form standing
over Old Man Bill in his chair.

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:46.370
You can see the oxygen tanks here, as if
Bill is down to his final moments and Valak

00:16:46.370 --> 00:16:48.280
is just waiting to feast on his soul.

00:16:48.280 --> 00:16:51.894
I’m not sure what it is, but there’s definitely
something creepy about The Nun’s face being

00:16:51.894 --> 00:16:52.465
blurred.

00:16:52.465 --> 00:16:55.250
The next subliminal image is on screen for
just two frames.

00:16:55.250 --> 00:16:56.800
Again, Valak’s face is blurred.

00:16:56.800 --> 00:16:59.050
This is the hallway scene I discussed earlier.

00:16:59.050 --> 00:17:02.740
Shortly after that, is this very unsettling
image of the Annabelle doll sitting in the

00:17:02.740 --> 00:17:03.740
dark.

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:07.000
This was probably here to tease Annabelle
Creation, which came out the year after The

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:08.000
Conjuring 2.

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:12.279
The final image to flash on screen is this
one, of Bill Wilkins possessed by the glowing

00:17:12.279 --> 00:17:16.241
eyes of Valak, leaving the film on
a very chilling note despite the happy ending,

00:17:16.241 --> 00:17:19.939
and setting up for the spin-off that would
come out in 2018, The Nun.

00:17:19.939 --> 00:17:23.620
So with that, I’ve now released a Things
You Missed episode on every Conjuring Universe

00:17:23.620 --> 00:17:27.419
film to date, so click that playlist on the
left to make sure you’re up to date on everything

00:17:27.419 --> 00:17:30.559
you missed in The Conjuring, Annabelle, The
Nun and La Llorona.

00:17:30.559 --> 00:17:33.781
Of course, you know I’ll be covering The
Conjuring 3 as soon as it’s available, so

00:17:33.781 --> 00:17:38.220
make sure you subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every week, ring the deathbell for

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:41.161
notifications and I’ll see you in the next one.

00:17:41.161 --> 00:17:43.902
Assuming we both survive.

00:17:43.902 --> 00:17:45.798
*weird growling noise*

